WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.420
Can you name a ring which isn't round?

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.300
A Boxing ring!

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.740
As grand as the Olympic games are,

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:11.460
it has its fair share of myths and controversies.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:16.200
One such popular myth revolves around its flag or symbols.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.100
We know that the flag comprises of 5 rings

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.140
of different colours on a white background.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:26.220
This is believed to represent the 5 participating continents,

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.380
but that is not entirely true!

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.740
Originally designed by Pierre de Coubertin,

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.460
the 5 interlaced rings were meant to represent

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.160
the number of participating continents, which were five.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:48.320
But each colour did not represent any particular continent.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:49.320
Hold on,

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.600
do we have only 5 colours in consideration here?

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:56.360
Nope, one important thing many of us wouldn’t have noticed

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:58.720
is that there are six colours in the flag,

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.340
including white, which is the background.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.660
So why these 6 colours?

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:06.280
The six colours were chosen from the flags

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:09.540
of the participating countries of that era!

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:11.580
Blue and yellow of Sweden,

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.700
blue and white of Greece,

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.720
red and white of England,

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.600
and tricolour flags of Germany and Italy

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:21.640
and the flags of other countries as well!

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.700
So, taking into account all these colours,

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.440
the Olympic flag was designed this way!

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.500
Now you know what the Olympic flag represents

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.500
and the idea behind it.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:35.200
Have you ever wondered what might be the idea

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.800
behind the selection of various games at Olympics?

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.080
How are these games selected?

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:44.940
The first step in the process of becoming an Olympic sport

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:49.860
would be its recognition as a sport by the International Olympic committee.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:53.780
So if any sport gets recognized by IOC

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.840
then does it qualify as an Olympic sport?

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.260
Not really.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.220
For example, Chess and Bowling are recognized sports,

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:05.500
but are not conducted under the banner of Olympics.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:09.540
So what are the other criteria that a game needs to fulfil?

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.420
Well, its your Kyu box to explore!

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:16.260
Let us know about your findings in the comments section.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.920
And you have to subscribe to our channel.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:22.260
to get notified about the new uploads on our channel.

